  <section|Read sources><label|read-sources>

  Scott/part2/I-section.tex:1\U553, through the regulator, rate transfer,
  trace coefficient, all-radius squeeze and finite Wick obstruction.
  Martin/existence/trace-asymptotic.tex:1\U115 checked for
  ordered-quarter-square normalization and the distinction between Ward and
  running-coupling normalization. The bounded source packet in
  blueprint/continuum-chapters.md lists detailed remaining suppliers.

  <section|Literature><label|literature>

  Verified original APS publisher page DOI 10.1103/PhysRevD.16.438 for
  Collins\UDuncan\UJoglekar (1977), metadata and abstract. Publisher full
  text requires authorization (harvest endpoint returned401). Citation is
  restricted to perturbative provenance, not a claimed proof of this
  constructive trace law. The direct Laplace profile expansion is a standard
  application of the asymptotic methods already cited to Wong; it is not
  claimed as a new theorem.

  <section|Status><label|status>

  The chapter proves the finite-dimensional stability implication, tensor
  cancellation given the stated rate input, the all-radius consequence given
  prescribed-radius comparison, and the precisely defined finite mass-shell
  profile obstruction. It explicitly does NOT claim to have supplied the
  quantitative current transfer and regulator estimates. Those require the
  same actual Hessian/current, projection, matching and marked family as
  preceding chapters.

  The gap between qualitative comparison and an amplified trace is quantified
  by e_i=M_i^(1/5), q_i=M_i^(1/6), q_i/e_i-\<gtr\>0. The equation-direction
  rate and trace-as-forward-difference rate have different origins. No
  differentiation of a bounded asymptotic error is used; a mean-value
  selection at fixed regulator interval precedes the small-regulator limit.

  <section|Remaining work><label|remaining-work>

  Expand and verify the finite-cutoff current transfer from its explicit
  lattice kernels, regulated contact identity and weighted estimates;
  establish uniform prescribed-radius windows from actual marked Gaussian
  comparison; match terminal/current normalizations to the common field
  quotient. Verify these with an independent reviewer before removing the
  conditional theorem labels. No mass gap or exclusion of arbitrary
  generalized free fields is asserted.

  Integrated compilation and visual review pending; independent review
  requested from continuum agent after its Chapter14 corrections.
